      "text": "Vignesh vs The Deptuy Director Health Officer on 25 March, \n2024 \nAuthor: D.Bharatha Chakravarthy\nBench: Sanjay V.Gangapurwala, D.Bharatha Chakravarthy\n Wp No.1825 of\n In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras\n Dated: 25.03.2024\n Coram\n The Hon'Ble Mr.Sanjay V.Gangapurwala, Chief Justice\n And\n The Hon'Ble Mr.Justice D.Bharatha Chakravarthy\n Wp No.1825 of 2024\n Vignesh .. Petitioner \n -vs-\n 1. The Deptuy Director Health Officer,\n Thamaraipakkam Road, Ekkadu,\n Thiruvallur District. \n 2. The Food Safety Officer,\n Food Safety, Second Floor, \n Collectorate Office, Thiruvallur, \n Thiruvallur District . \n 3. The Revenue Divisional Officer,\n Thiruvallur, Thiruvallur District. \n 4. The Tahsildar,\n Poonamallee Taluk, Poonamallee. \n 5. The Block Development Officer,\n Poonamallee B.D.O. Office,\n Poonamallee, Chennai. \n 6. The Inspector of Police,\n Poonamallee Police Station,\n Poonamallee, Chennai. \n Page 1 of 4\nVignesh vs The Deptuy Director Health Officer on 25 March, 2024\nIndian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/164016774/\n1\n\nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis\n\n Wp  \n 7. Bhavani  8. Annamalai .. R  Prayer: Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of Ind  issuance of a Writ of Mandamus directing the respondents 1 to 6 to  remove the encroachment made by the respondents 7 and 8 in front of  the petitioner's shop at No.3/159A, Thandarai Main Road,\n Pidarithangal, Banavedu Thottam, Poonamallee Taluk, Tiruvallur  District based on the petitioner's representations dated 08.12.2022  22.12.2022 and 09.10.2023. \n For the Petitioner : Mr.P.Krishnan  For the Respondents : Mr.P.Harish  Govt. Advocate for RR 1 to 5  : Mr.S.Sugendran  Addl. Public Prosecutor for R  : Not ready in notice reg. RR 7  **** *\n ORDER (Made by the Hon'ble Chief Justice) In view of the fact that the petitioner has already filed a civil suit bearing O.S.No.29 of 2023 for the same relief, we are not inclined to pass any further orders in the writ petition. It is for the petitioner to prosecute the said suit. The petitioner may request the Court where https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis the suit is pending for its expeditious disposal, which request may be considered by the Court on its own merits.\nThe writ petition is, accordingly, disposed of. There shall be no order as to costs. \n (S.V.G., CJ.) \n 25.03.2024  Index : Yes/No  Neutral Citation : Yes/No  sra  To Vignesh vs The Deptuy Director Health Officer on 25 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/164016774/\n2 1. The Deptuy Director Health Officer, Thamaraipakkam Road, Ekkadu, Thiruvallur District. \n2. The Food Safety Officer, Food Safety, Second Floor, Collectorate Office, Thiruvallur, Thiruvallur District. \n3. The Revenue Divisional Officer, Thiruvallur, Thiruvallur District. \n4. The Tahsildar, Poonamallee Taluk, Poonamallee.\n5. The Block Development Officer, Poonamallee B.D.O. Office, Poonamallee, Chennai. \nhttps://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis THE HON'BLE CHIEF JUSTICE AND D.BHARATHA CHAKRAVARTHY, J. \n(sra) \n6. The Inspector of Police, Poonamallee Police Station, Poonamallee, Chennai. \n25.03.2024 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis Vignesh vs The Deptuy Director Health Officer on 25 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/164016774/\n3",
